WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.920 --> 00:00:06.160
Disney has produced dozens of animated classics
over the year, all of them packed with memorable

00:00:06.180 --> 00:00:06.680
images.

00:00:06.980 --> 00:00:11.100
There are some images, though, that we just
have to linger on longer than others.

00:00:11.300 --> 00:00:14.940
Here are some of the most memorable Disney
movie moments that will make you say "Did

00:00:14.940 --> 00:00:19.300
I just see what I thought I saw?," pick up
the remote, and hit pause.

00:00:20.280 --> 00:00:25.840
Released in 2003, Finding Nemo follows the
story of a little clownfish who is separated

00:00:25.840 --> 00:00:28.780
from his father and desperately tries to get
back home.

00:00:28.940 --> 00:00:34.020
This Disney/Pixar classic was a massive hit
at the box office and became an instant success

00:00:34.020 --> 00:00:34.920
on home video.

00:00:35.220 --> 00:00:39.340
Clearly, it was seen by lots and lots of people,
many of them more than once.

00:00:39.480 --> 00:00:40.900
"Just keep swimming.

00:00:40.910 --> 00:00:42.190
Just keep swimming.

00:00:42.190 --> 00:00:44.260
Just keep swimming, swimming, swimming."

00:00:44.820 --> 00:00:49.680
That said, it wasn't until many years after
Finding Nemo's release that many viewers noticed

00:00:49.680 --> 00:00:50.880
one key detail.

00:00:51.360 --> 00:00:55.720
During Nemo's journey, he ends up in the fish
tank at a dentist's office.

00:00:55.730 --> 00:01:00.050
When he wakes up in the tank, the camera pans
around the dentist's waiting room, showing

00:01:00.050 --> 00:01:02.580
what Nemo can see from his watery vantage
point.

00:01:03.280 --> 00:01:07.800
The view shows some toys lying on the floor,
and one of them happens to be a familiar face.

00:01:08.380 --> 00:01:12.700
It's Buzz Lightyear, who made his first movie
appearance in Pixar's Toy Story, eight years

00:01:12.700 --> 00:01:13.200
earlier.

00:01:13.380 --> 00:01:18.200
Pixar is fond of leaving Easter eggs for its
viewers to find, and since this one involves

00:01:18.210 --> 00:01:22.840
two of the most popular and heartwarming Disney
films ever made, it's exciting to pause the

00:01:22.840 --> 00:01:25.400
movie long enough to spot Buzz Lightyear's
cameo.

00:01:26.520 --> 00:01:32.520
Originally released in 1996, The Hunchback
of Notre Dame follows the story of Quasimodo,

00:01:32.520 --> 00:01:35.760
a man who is rejected by his people because
of his deformity.

00:01:36.340 --> 00:01:42.420
Quasimodo lives in a tower of Notre Dame Cathedral
in Paris, where he serves as the bell-ringer

00:01:42.420 --> 00:01:46.140
and spends his days in solitude wishing for
someone to share his life with.

00:01:46.460 --> 00:01:50.720
At the beginning of the movie, Quasimodo sings
the song "Out There" from the top of Notre

00:01:50.720 --> 00:01:51.820
Dame cathedral.

00:01:52.180 --> 00:01:57.320
The camera pans along the street below, and
as it moves, we can see a man shaking out

00:01:57.320 --> 00:01:58.300
a piece of fabric.

00:01:58.580 --> 00:02:03.030
Look closely, and you'll see it's the magic
flying carpet that Disney fans will recognize

00:02:03.030 --> 00:02:03.880
from Aladdin.

00:02:04.140 --> 00:02:08.460
If that isn't enough to make you pause, here
are two bonuses: If you look closely enough,

00:02:08.460 --> 00:02:11.980
you'll also see Belle from Beauty and the
Beast walking by with a book.

00:02:12.920 --> 00:02:18.600
Aladdin is a charming 1992 Disney movie that
follows a street urchin who discovers a genie

00:02:18.609 --> 00:02:21.219
in a lamp and has his wishes fulfilled.

00:02:21.219 --> 00:02:26.249
But things aren't always as they seem, and
Aladdin must fight an evil sorcerer to save

00:02:26.249 --> 00:02:28.160
his love interest Princess Jasmine.

00:02:28.560 --> 00:02:33.360
Aladdin was released shortly after another
Disney classic from the same era, Beauty and

00:02:33.380 --> 00:02:34.040
the Beast.

00:02:34.220 --> 00:02:38.320
Both films were extremely successful, though
Beauty and the Beast might be considered the

00:02:38.320 --> 00:02:39.380
greater classic now.

00:02:39.520 --> 00:02:42.340
Still, the two movies are connected by more
than the calendar.

00:02:42.880 --> 00:02:47.540
In one scene in Aladdin, we see Jasmine's
father, the Sultan, playing with a stack of

00:02:47.540 --> 00:02:48.040
toys.

00:02:48.300 --> 00:02:53.420
Look closely and you'll see that one of these
toys is actually a model of The Beast from

00:02:53.420 --> 00:02:54.420
Beauty and the Beast.

00:02:55.360 --> 00:03:00.780
Oscar-winning 1989 Disney classic The Little
Mermaid has one scene that's chock-full of

00:03:00.780 --> 00:03:03.900
cameos from characters seen in the studio's
other movies.

00:03:03.980 --> 00:03:07.880
There are so many, in fact, that you'll definitely
want to hit pause and count.

00:03:08.680 --> 00:03:13.800
During the scene featuring King Triton's entrance,
four other Disney characters are visible:

00:03:13.800 --> 00:03:18.540
Mickey Mouse, Goofy, and Donald Duck can be
seen near the bottom left of the screen.

00:03:18.960 --> 00:03:22.140
It's a quick cameo, though, since King Triton
is moving so quickly.

00:03:22.560 --> 00:03:26.380
If you really want to spot the characters,
you'll have to quickly pause and take a close

00:03:26.400 --> 00:03:26.920
look.

00:03:27.020 --> 00:03:29.800
Future Disney acquisition Kermit the Frog
is there, too.

00:03:30.380 --> 00:03:34.659
You can even spot the Warner Bros. character
Mr. Limpet in The Little Mermaid.

00:03:34.660 --> 00:03:38.120
He pops up near the end of the classic musical
number "Under the Sea."

00:03:38.460 --> 00:03:44.279
A bit of a lesser-known character, he was
played by Don Knotts, who starred in the 1964

00:03:44.280 --> 00:03:49.140
live-action/animated hybrid The Incredible
Mr. Limpet, about a man who is turned into

00:03:49.140 --> 00:03:49.640
a fish.

00:03:50.040 --> 00:03:53.760
Clearly, there was plenty of room under the
sea for the animators of The Little Mermaid

00:03:53.760 --> 00:03:57.740
to show some love to as many characters as
they wanted from Disney and beyond.

00:03:58.900 --> 00:04:04.720
The animated Disney film 101 Dalmatians was
first released in 1961, and remains a beloved

00:04:04.720 --> 00:04:05.220
classic.

00:04:05.760 --> 00:04:11.510
It's the story of an unlikely, and truly massive,
family of dogs that find themselves the target

00:04:11.510 --> 00:04:15.000
of an evil, fur-loving woman named Cruella
de Vil.

00:04:15.260 --> 00:04:20.259
Because of the adorable heroes in the film,
and Cruella's place as one of Disney's best-loved

00:04:20.260 --> 00:04:23.540
villains, fans keep coming back to 101 Dalmatians.

00:04:23.940 --> 00:04:28.620
But it turns out the dogs of the title are
far from the only Disney pups present in the

00:04:28.620 --> 00:04:29.120
film.

00:04:29.660 --> 00:04:34.199
A third of the way through the film, dogs
all across London are participating in the

00:04:34.199 --> 00:04:38.729
"twilight bark," barking to each other across
the city to spread the word that the Dalmatians

00:04:38.729 --> 00:04:39.300
need help.

00:04:39.729 --> 00:04:45.060
In this scene we can see Jock, Bull, Peg,
Lady, and the Tramp, all characters from Disney's

00:04:45.060 --> 00:04:47.260
1955 film Lady and the Tramp.

00:04:47.660 --> 00:04:51.120
Jock, recognizable by his collar, comes out
of a doghouse.

00:04:51.120 --> 00:04:55.650
Bull and Peg, who were in Lady and the Tramp
as dogs in the pound, are sitting in the window

00:04:55.650 --> 00:04:56.380
of a pet store.

00:04:56.820 --> 00:05:02.380
And finally, after a car goes by, the Tramp
stands on top of a truck and Lady is on the

00:05:02.380 --> 00:05:02.880
street.

00:05:03.860 --> 00:05:09.940
Moana is a popular 2016 animated musical about
a Polynesian teenager who embarks on a journey

00:05:09.940 --> 00:05:11.920
to save her people and find herself.

00:05:12.300 --> 00:05:16.560
It's also packed with Easter eggs, including
one that incorporated a Frozen character.

00:05:17.180 --> 00:05:22.760
As Moana starts on her journey, she enlists
the help of Maui, a demigod who once owned

00:05:22.760 --> 00:05:23.580
a magical hook.

00:05:24.000 --> 00:05:27.400
The hook allows Maui to transform into any
animal he wants.

00:05:27.720 --> 00:05:32.479
During the middle of the movie, Maui recovers
his hook and uses it to swiftly transform

00:05:32.480 --> 00:05:33.900
from animal to animal.

00:05:34.000 --> 00:05:38.060
The transformation goes so fast that it's
a blink-and-miss-it type of scene.

00:05:38.069 --> 00:05:41.780
If you're really paying attention, though,
you'll see that one of the animals Maui transforms

00:05:41.780 --> 00:05:44.720
into is Sven, the lovable reindeer from Frozen.

00:05:45.020 --> 00:05:49.160
The scene is fast and definitely requires
a pause button to catch the reindeer, but

00:05:49.160 --> 00:05:53.300
the expression on his face is hilarious and
worth going back for a second look.

00:05:53.900 --> 00:05:59.479
The movie Big Hero 6, which hit theaters in
2014, is a superhero story about a robotics

00:05:59.479 --> 00:06:01.810
genius who lives in a futuristic city.

00:06:01.810 --> 00:06:07.550
The boy, Hiro Hamada, puts together a team
of superheroes in his attempt to catch a mysterious

00:06:07.550 --> 00:06:08.440
masked villain.

00:06:09.030 --> 00:06:13.840
In one scene, Hiro goes to the San Fransokyo
police station to file a report.

00:06:13.850 --> 00:06:18.219
Eagle-eyed viewers will notice a "Wanted"
poster hanging on the wall that features none

00:06:18.220 --> 00:06:22.080
other than Prince Hans, the villain of Disney's
2013 hit Frozen.

00:06:22.500 --> 00:06:26.660
This cameo was fairly easy to spot, since
the police station scene was featured in the

00:06:26.660 --> 00:06:27.160
movie's trailer.

00:06:27.260 --> 00:06:30.640
But Hans isn't the only Frozen character in
Big Hero 6.

00:06:31.220 --> 00:06:35.280
Others found their way into the film, too,
in places that were a little bit harder to

00:06:35.300 --> 00:06:35.800
spot.

00:06:36.100 --> 00:06:42.199
A ship from Arendelle, the name of the kingdom
in Frozen, and a shot of beloved snowman Olaf

00:06:42.200 --> 00:06:43.640
also made it into the movie.

00:06:43.920 --> 00:06:46.100
Just keep hitting pause until you catch 'em
all.

00:06:47.000 --> 00:06:52.360
The 2001 Pixar hit Monsters, Inc. tells the
tale of the biggest scare factory in the monster

00:06:52.370 --> 00:06:56.289
world, a little girl who visits from the human
world, and what happens next.

00:06:56.289 --> 00:07:01.000
Oh, and along the way, fellow Pixar favorite
Nemo makes a cameo too.

00:07:01.420 --> 00:07:05.349
At one point in the movie, we can see him
hanging on the wall in a bedroom as Sully

00:07:05.349 --> 00:07:08.060
and Mike try to get rid of the villainous
Randall.

00:07:08.060 --> 00:07:12.840
Later, Boo and hero monster Sully are in her
room together and she shows him a few of her

00:07:12.840 --> 00:07:15.160
favorite toys, including a stuffed Nemo.

00:07:15.800 --> 00:07:19.680
Here's the real kicker, though: When Monsters,
Inc. was released, Finding Nemo wasn't out

00:07:19.680 --> 00:07:20.180
yet.

00:07:20.480 --> 00:07:24.580
At the time Monsters, Inc. came out, audiences
probably didn't think anything about the little

00:07:24.580 --> 00:07:26.520
clownfish that popped up once or twice.

00:07:26.840 --> 00:07:30.720
Many years later, though, diehard fans of
Finding Nemo are fumbling for their remotes

00:07:30.720 --> 00:07:34.180
to hit that pause button and smile at the
sight of their favorite fish.

00:07:35.120 --> 00:07:40.540
Tangled is a 2010 movie telling the classic
story of Rapunzel with a few fresh twists.

00:07:40.540 --> 00:07:44.760
Rapunzel is still the girl who lives locked
away in a tower with her long flowing hair

00:07:44.760 --> 00:07:47.620
that can be used as a rope, but she's also
got big dreams.

00:07:48.060 --> 00:07:52.699
Rapunzel wants to get away from the tower,
and when a dashing bandit named Flynn shows

00:07:52.700 --> 00:07:56.120
up at her window one day, she sees her chance
to begin a new life.

00:07:56.360 --> 00:08:00.080
It's the start of an unlikely journey that's
packed with Disney adventure.

00:08:00.080 --> 00:08:02.569
There's something else in the film that's
unlikely, too.

00:08:02.569 --> 00:08:07.090
At the beginning of the movie in Rapunzel's
tower, one shot shows a spinning wheel behind

00:08:07.090 --> 00:08:07.780
the princess.

00:08:07.940 --> 00:08:13.300
It's the same spinning wheel from Sleeping
Beauty, the classic 1959 Disney movie.

00:08:13.309 --> 00:08:15.809
If you haven't caught this one before, though,
don't feel bad.

00:08:15.809 --> 00:08:19.830
Even diehard Disney fans have had to watch
the movie quite a few times to realize it's

00:08:19.830 --> 00:08:21.169
the same spinning wheel.

00:08:21.169 --> 00:08:25.699
Rapunzel's tower has items that relate to
other Disney princess movies, too.

00:08:25.699 --> 00:08:30.830
Use the pause button to look around and you'll
find Snow White's apple, Ariel's seashell,

00:08:30.830 --> 00:08:32.820
Belle's rose, and Cinderella's slipper.

00:08:33.820 --> 00:08:39.780
WALL-E is a 2008 movie about a lonely little
robot left behind on Earth to collect junk

00:08:39.780 --> 00:08:44.140
after the human race abandons the ruined planet
in search of a new home.

00:08:44.460 --> 00:08:48.440
At the beginning of the movie, as viewers
are being introduced to WALL-E and his daily

00:08:48.449 --> 00:08:53.880
life, the robot comes home after work and
the camera shows several items he's collected.

00:08:53.880 --> 00:08:57.580
If you look closely, you might see a familiar
face peeking out from behind a couple of bowling

00:08:57.580 --> 00:08:58.080
pins.

00:08:58.560 --> 00:09:04.480
It's Rex, the lovable and anxious dinosaur
from the 1995 hit Toy Story and its sequels.

00:09:04.490 --> 00:09:07.829
"I just don't think I can take that kind of
rejection!"

00:09:07.829 --> 00:09:09.890
The scene is honestly a little sad.

00:09:09.890 --> 00:09:12.340
After all, WALL-E is the last robot left on
earth.

00:09:12.940 --> 00:09:15.180
The planet is a pretty empty, lonely place.

00:09:15.600 --> 00:09:18.000
Did Rex just get thrown away to die alone?

00:09:18.010 --> 00:09:20.540
It seems like an injustice to the poor dinosaur.

00:09:20.540 --> 00:09:25.260
But at least he has WALL-E. As they say, one
man's trash is another robot's treasure.

00:09:26.480 --> 00:09:33.000
Pocahontas, released in 1995, tells the loosely
fact-based story of Native American princess

00:09:33.010 --> 00:09:36.790
Pocahontas and English settler Captain John
Smith.

00:09:36.790 --> 00:09:41.620
When the two fall in love, Pocahontas's father,
the chief of her tribe, doesn't approve.

00:09:41.860 --> 00:09:46.480
To further complicate matters, the other settlers
who arrived with Smith are plotting to steal

00:09:46.480 --> 00:09:47.830
gold from the Native Americans.

00:09:47.830 --> 00:09:53.040
At the beginning of the movie, there's a scene
during which Pocahontas leaps off of a cliff

00:09:53.040 --> 00:09:57.220
in a majestic swan dive, entering the water
with only a small splash.

00:09:57.760 --> 00:10:01.180
Although not entirely realistic, her swan
dive is beautiful.

00:10:01.260 --> 00:10:05.420
As a kid, it's fun to hit the pause button
and see if you can catch Pocahontas right

00:10:05.420 --> 00:10:06.420
in the middle of her leap.

00:10:06.800 --> 00:10:08.800
Just don't try to recreate this scene at home.

00:10:09.420 --> 00:10:14.440
Disney's Cinderella came out in 1950 and has been delighting audiences of all ages ever

00:10:14.440 --> 00:10:15.440
since.

00:10:15.660 --> 00:10:20.600
The tale of a girl trying to escape her stepmother's
cruelty and then attending the royal ball

00:10:20.610 --> 00:10:22.579
with Prince Charming is a classic.

00:10:22.580 --> 00:10:24.980
But Cinderella has a second claim to fame,
too.

00:10:25.060 --> 00:10:29.340
The castle featured in the movie is the same
castle that forms the basis for Walt Disney

00:10:29.340 --> 00:10:30.200
Pictures' logo.

00:10:30.540 --> 00:10:35.400
What started as a simple graphic of white
lines has since become a beautiful three-dimensional

00:10:35.400 --> 00:10:37.480
rendering at the beginning of every Disney
film.

00:10:37.980 --> 00:10:41.880
You can also visit the castle any time you
want at Walt Disney World, where it serves

00:10:41.880 --> 00:10:44.000
as the centerpiece of the Magic Kingdom.

00:10:44.380 --> 00:10:48.000
Next time you watch Cinderella, it's worth
hitting the pause button during the scene

00:10:48.000 --> 00:10:51.100
when we first see the castle to see how familiar
it seems.

00:10:51.900 --> 00:10:53.660
Check out one of our newest videos right here!

00:10:53.780 --> 00:10:57.100
Plus, even more Looper videos about your favorite
films are coming soon.

00:10:57.260 --> 00:11:00.320
Subscribe to our YouTube channel and hit the
bell so you don't miss a single one.

